    "created_at": "2016-04-26T18:55:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-26T18:55:10Z",
    "body": "> the default origin\n\nThis one's interesting. @annevk clarified in IRC this is \"the origin for fetching when none is specified is from the client.\"\n\nFor classic workers there is no difference, since you can only fetch a same-origin classic worker. Module workers allow CORS though. It seems pretty clear that the fetching should use the calling document's origin.\n\nI am tenatively starting to think, based on the so-far-fairly-contradictory evidence presented, that it would be best to change workers to use the current settings object inside the Worker constructor, and pass that along to \"run a worker\", instead of passing along a referrer and using the newly-created settings object.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
